Anaïs Marchal is a late 20s human male, with red hair and dark brown eyes. He's the fraternal twin of [[Anouk Marchal|Anouk]]. Anaïs often wears sharp, plain suits but adorns his fingers and wrists with wooden rings and bracelets. He has a moderately sized raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]].

Anaïs is the more magically-inclined of the twins. His portion of the [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] workshop is dominated by magical tomes and alchemical reagents. He tends to be more reserved than his sister.

Between Anaïs and her sister [[Anouk Marchal|Anouk]], no small amount of hard-won experience stands behind them — seasoned adventurers both, and formidable for it.

Anouk asked the Party at the [[Sin and Tonic]] to look for Anaïs, who had gone out two days earlier on the trail of a [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] lead and had not returned. They found him in a one-room cabin at void 26 in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]], his hands shackled to a metal cot and a metal band locked over his mouth, [[Aut]]'s three-dot mark above the door. He took them for Aut's spies and kicked [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] across the room before they freed him.

He had followed a report from a convox sensor of a blip with the same harmonics as the Voidsong, and the blip was a lure. He believes a friend of Aut's in the church set it to catch anyone listening in.

Anaïs serves [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]] the Fickle Mistress, as does his sister. He has not spoken with her in years, and says she gives little direction and may grant a great boon or a terrible bane. He told the Party about the five narrative siblings, blamed Aut for [[Geography/Raelion/index|Raelion]], [[Geography/Brithwyn/index|Brithwyn]] and the Plaguebearer, and recognized [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]] among the six gods said to be coming. He says he is made of skin, though a hard armoured thing sits behind his head where a skull would be, and he has been 35 for nine months. He offered to meet the Party at the pilgrimage on Saturday with Anouk, and threatened to kill them if they sold the twins out to Aut.

When the Party brought down [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]]'s drug works with him, Anaïs and his sister came to the works in a car they had rammed into the side of the building and fought their way through Sbrtlby's meat shields. They walked out unhurt from a sphere that turned the falling building aside, and rode back to the [[Sin and Tonic]] with the Party. He knows about the vaccine the Party carry; his sister did not.
